purge_entities.description:
This will remove {count} Vaillant eBUS entities that no entity provides any more (for example a zone or register the controller no longer reports), and Vaillant eBUS devices left without entities.

{entities}

It will also switch off {dormant_count} enabled entities that have no data and that a new installation would not switch on (for example a sensor for hardware you do not have). They are not deleted. Each one switches on again by itself when its register returns a value.

{dormant}

Entities that you renamed, hid, labelled or assigned to an area are kept ({kept}).

confirm.description:
{count} Vaillant eBUS entities exist in Home Assistant that the integration no longer provides, for example from a zone or register the controller no longer reports. Submit removes them, and any Vaillant eBUS device left empty.

{entities}

Also, {dormant_count} enabled entities have no data and a new installation would not switch them on, for example a sensor for hardware you do not have. Submit also switches them off. They are not deleted, and each one switches on again by itself when its register returns a value.

{dormant}

Entities that you renamed, hid, labelled or assigned to an area are kept ({kept}). Nothing changes before you select Submit.
